WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 0: Alphabet & Sounds.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:12.688
You will meet all the letters of the alphabet — big letters
and small letters — and learn the sound each one makes.

3
00:00:12.768 --> 00:00:20.469
You will trace letters, say their sounds, and blend
them into your first little words like cat and sun.

4
00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:25.531
You will also learn your first
sight words and read tiny sentences.

5
00:00:25.611 --> 00:00:30.894
Take your time: knowing your letters
well matters more than going fast.

6
00:00:30.974 --> 00:00:37.240
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:44.618
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
recognise and name uppercase and lowercase letters.

8
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:49.536
You will also connect letters
a-z with their most common sounds.

9
00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:54.301
You will also hear and say beginning sounds in familiar words.

10
00:00:54.381 --> 00:00:57.145
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:57.225 --> 00:01:02.797
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: apple, ball, cat, dog, elephant, fish.

12
00:01:02.877 --> 00:01:08.248
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

13
00:01:08.328 --> 00:01:12.487
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

14
00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:18.954
The reading sequence includes Week 1: Learn the
Alphabet (A–Z) and Week 2: Phonics (Letter Sounds a–m).

15
00:01:19.034 --> 00:01:19.833
Read actively.

16
00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:24.164
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

17
00:01:24.244 --> 00:01:28.245
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

18
00:01:28.325 --> 00:01:31.771
The first language focus is The letter A says aaa.

19
00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:34.520
Say the aaa sound, not the letter name.

20
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.976
Open your mouth wide, like Sami saying a-a-apple.

21
00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:45.661
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

22
00:01:45.741 --> 00:01:48.880
In speaking, you will complete Sound and say 1.

23
00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.468
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

24
00:01:53.548 --> 00:01:56.960
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

25
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.589
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

26
00:02:00.669 --> 00:02:02.219
You are ready to begin.

27
00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:09.231
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

28
00:02:09.311 --> 00:02:12.631
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

29
00:02:12.711 --> 00:02:20.494
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
